WEBVTT

00:15.856 --> 00:17.818
(MUFFLED RUMBLING)

00:22.291 --> 00:24.495
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

00:32.069 --> 00:33.039
(DOOR CLOSES)

00:33.141 --> 00:35.609
(MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING
OVER SPEAKERS)

00:35.711 --> 00:37.309
How can I help you?

00:37.411 --> 00:38.874
(IN BRITISH ACCENT) Uh,
can I get a black coffee?

00:38.976 --> 00:40.643
Sure.

00:46.754 --> 00:47.722
Thank you.

00:47.824 --> 00:49.316
(INDISTINCT CHATTER, LAUGHTER)

00:49.418 --> 00:51.588
(INTRIGUING MUSIC PLAYING)

00:56.291 --> 00:57.825
(MUSIC STOPS)

00:59.034 --> 01:00.267
-(CHAIR SLIDES)
-(MUSIC RESUMES)

01:05.439 --> 01:08.206
-(MUSIC, CHATTER QUIETENS)
-(MUFFLED BUZZING)

01:08.308 --> 01:10.475
(INDISTINCT CHATTER,
LAUGHTER RESUMES)

01:13.049 --> 01:15.216
-(CHATTER QUIETENS)
-(MUFFLED BUZZING)

01:15.949 --> 01:18.153
(CHATTER RESUMES)

01:19.022 --> 01:21.189
(INTRIGUING MUSIC
CONTINUES PLAYING)

01:26.158 --> 01:27.327
(CAMERA SHUTTER CLICKS)

01:38.635 --> 01:40.802
(INTRIGUING MUSIC
CONTINUES PLAYING)

01:50.345 --> 01:51.516
(CHAIR SLIDES)

01:52.151 --> 01:53.782
(FAINT, MUFFLED BUZZING)

01:54.317 --> 01:56.023
(CLEARS THROAT)

01:56.125 --> 01:58.089
I love that book so much.
It's, uh...

01:58.191 --> 01:59.289
I just finished it last week.

01:59.391 --> 02:01.291
It's incredible.
It's... (STUTTERS)

02:01.393 --> 02:04.529
I really, really,
really admire it.

02:04.964 --> 02:05.863
And, uh...

02:05.965 --> 02:07.268
(CUP CLANGING)

02:08.972 --> 02:10.067
-(DOOR OPENS)
-(LOUD CHATTER)

02:10.169 --> 02:11.536
(CLEARS THROAT) Uh...

02:12.735 --> 02:15.006
(SOFTLY) All right.
(CLEARS THROAT)

02:15.108 --> 02:17.311
(INTRIGUING MUSIC PLAYING)

02:23.550 --> 02:25.512
(STUTTERING)
Um, I'm sorry. I didn't mean...

02:25.615 --> 02:28.556
(ROMANTIC '80s POP MUSIC
PLAYING)

02:28.658 --> 02:30.517
(MUFFLED SPEECH)

02:30.620 --> 02:32.060
CHARLIE: I wasn't... Genuinely,

02:32.162 --> 02:33.223
-I really admire the book.
-What? Sorry?

02:33.325 --> 02:34.829
I was just saying, I'm not...

02:34.931 --> 02:36.698
I'm not hitting on you. I...

02:36.800 --> 02:37.725
Sorry, what do you mean?

02:37.827 --> 02:39.595
Genuinely,
I just really admire the book.

02:39.697 --> 02:41.934
(INDISTINCT CHATTER
CONTINUES IN BACKGROUND)

02:42.036 --> 02:43.032
I'm deaf in this one.

02:43.134 --> 02:44.135
You're deaf?

02:44.238 --> 02:46.773
Yeah. This one though. I can...

02:46.875 --> 02:49.306
(LAUGHS AWKWARDLY)

02:49.408 --> 02:51.675
-(EMMA CHUCKLES SOFTLY)
-Uh...

02:54.917 --> 02:57.352
Yeah, the, uh... (SIGHS)

02:57.854 --> 02:58.814
Do you want to start over?

03:00.651 --> 03:03.055
-Um...
-We could just try it again?

03:03.157 --> 03:04.455
-Maybe?
-You wanna try...

03:04.557 --> 03:06.393
-Just do it again?
-EMMA: Yeah. Do it again.

03:08.559 --> 03:09.924
-Okay.
-Okay. (CHUCKLES SOFTLY)

03:19.073 --> 03:21.108
(UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING)

03:21.210 --> 03:23.404
CHARLIE:
 "I was absolutely certain

03:23.506 --> 03:25.077
 "I was being trapped

03:25.179 --> 03:26.610
"and that you were recording me

03:26.712 --> 03:29.213
 "and I was gonna be
 all over the Internet,

03:29.315 --> 03:30.812
 "but I now understand..."

03:30.914 --> 03:33.349
"...that the only thing
that could have saved me

03:33.451 --> 03:34.921
"was a second first impression."

03:35.023 --> 03:36.618
Yeah. So funny. Great.

03:36.720 --> 03:38.323
So I'm gonna start there
and then go on

03:38.425 --> 03:39.720
 -to the first date.
-MIKE: Good.

03:39.822 --> 03:41.761
EMMA: So what'd you think
of the ending?

03:41.863 --> 03:42.756
Ending? Of what?

03:42.858 --> 03:44.291
EMMA: Of the book.
I just finished it.

03:44.393 --> 03:45.696
Oh, the, um...

03:45.798 --> 03:48.969
I don't know. I feel like
I didn't get it, you know.

03:49.071 --> 03:51.304
Like I was missing something.

03:51.406 --> 03:52.701
Yeah, no, I know what you mean.
I think...

03:52.804 --> 03:54.407
Yeah, me neither, really.
(CHUCKLES NERVOUSLY)

03:54.509 --> 03:56.770
'Cause did she die?
Is that... (CHUCKLES SOFTLY)

03:56.872 --> 03:58.544
Like, do you think
that's what it was?

03:59.509 --> 04:01.382
I think so. I think so.

04:02.350 --> 04:03.780
Just, that doesn't make
any sense.

04:04.380 --> 04:05.750
It doesn't?

04:05.852 --> 04:07.615
Well, no, 'cause you remember
this, like, the mirror thing?

04:07.717 --> 04:09.687
CHARLIE: Hm.
Wait, which mirror?

04:10.722 --> 04:13.420
The whole thing at the end
with the mirror.

04:13.522 --> 04:15.892
Um... (SMACKS LIPS)

04:15.994 --> 04:19.963
I thought it was just more of
a kind of metaphor for like...

04:20.065 --> 04:21.600
Uh...

04:21.702 --> 04:24.432
I just didn't really realize
it was real in the sense

04:24.534 --> 04:27.368
that the mirror was, um...

04:27.470 --> 04:28.910
The mirror was...

04:29.012 --> 04:30.408
(SIGHS) I don't even know...

04:30.510 --> 04:31.541
I don't even know
where to take this.

04:31.643 --> 04:33.981
I didn't read the book.
And, um... yeah.

04:34.084 --> 04:35.609
-What?
-I think I just glitched

04:35.711 --> 04:37.646
when I saw you... (STUTTERS)

04:37.748 --> 04:39.516
...and I just wanted
to talk to you.

04:39.618 --> 04:42.753
And I didn't have anything,
so...

04:43.793 --> 04:44.788
That's weird.

04:48.991 --> 04:50.899
Um, yeah, I'm...
Well, I'm sorry. I didn't...

04:51.001 --> 04:52.829
Just a weird, little freak.

04:53.663 --> 04:55.331
Weird, little British freak.

04:55.433 --> 04:56.701
-Oh, yeah?
-(CHUCKLES)

04:56.803 --> 04:59.006
I'm sorry. I didn't realize
you actually doubled down.

04:59.108 --> 05:00.505
Yeah, what was I supposed to do?

05:00.607 --> 05:02.477
-How about reading the book?
-(CHARLIE SIGHS)

05:02.579 --> 05:05.340
For a first date? I don't know.
That's a lot weirder, no?

05:05.442 --> 05:07.446
How is that weirder?

05:07.549 --> 05:10.116
I don't know.
It just feels weirder somehow.

05:10.218 --> 05:12.048
Okay. Don't agree, but go on.

05:12.151 --> 05:13.188
(CHUCKLES)

05:13.290 --> 05:16.850
So, I wanna say this thing
about her laugh.

05:16.952 --> 05:18.458
Do you know
how it's kind of like...

05:18.560 --> 05:20.992
It's very cute,
but it's also kind of like...

05:21.094 --> 05:24.165
(CHORTLING)

05:24.267 --> 05:26.027
-Repulsive even. Okay.
-CHARLIE: Yeah.

05:26.129 --> 05:29.237
And then if, uh, she laughs,
then I can point it out

05:29.339 --> 05:30.637
and be like,
"And there it is!" you know.

05:30.739 --> 05:32.338
I did. I said, "If everyone
knows he's a piece of shit,

05:32.440 --> 05:33.875
"then why are we doing
a retrospective

05:33.977 --> 05:34.836
"in the first place?"

05:34.939 --> 05:36.738
It's like, it's so incredibly
irresponsible.

05:36.840 --> 05:38.511
No one ever cares
until it's too late.

05:38.613 --> 05:40.547
And then it always ends up
backfiring on me...

05:44.320 --> 05:45.947
Emma, I'm being serious.
It's not funny.

05:46.049 --> 05:48.852
No, I agree with you.
This is not funny at all.

05:50.025 --> 05:51.492
It's very serious.

05:53.863 --> 05:54.993
(SNICKERS)

05:55.095 --> 05:55.956
You're laughing.

05:56.059 --> 05:57.858
CHARLIE: "I love how you
 always find a way

05:57.960 --> 06:00.901
 "to turn my drama
 into a comedy."

06:01.003 --> 06:02.299
And then, uh...

06:02.401 --> 06:03.765
-I don't know.
-What?

06:03.867 --> 06:05.967
I kind of wanna
say something about...

06:06.069 --> 06:09.139
-(MOANING IN PLEASURE)
-(RATTLING, CLATTERING)

06:09.241 --> 06:10.578
-No.
-No?

06:10.680 --> 06:12.780
Why do you want to talk about
fucking in front of your family?

06:12.882 --> 06:13.677
Or her family?

06:13.779 --> 06:15.041
No, I don't wanna
say it, like, directly.

06:15.143 --> 06:17.419
I just wanna kind of allude
to it somehow

06:17.521 --> 06:21.554
'cause I just think
we've always had this sort of...

06:21.656 --> 06:24.386
Like an incredible chemistry
that's just... I...

06:24.488 --> 06:25.760
Yeah, no, do that.

06:25.862 --> 06:27.358
Do exactly that.

06:27.461 --> 06:29.794
-Okay?
-Okay, what if I said...

06:30.361 --> 06:31.425
licentious.

06:31.527 --> 06:34.068
Or languorous.

06:34.171 --> 06:35.062
Just skip this part completely.

06:35.164 --> 06:37.068
What, and just go straight
to the crying thing?

06:37.170 --> 06:39.771
(EMMA SOBBING)

06:40.976 --> 06:42.444
(SHUDDERS)

06:43.043 --> 06:44.039
(SIGHS)

06:44.673 --> 06:45.675
It's just, you know,

06:45.777 --> 06:47.008
it's my first time
saying it out loud,

06:47.110 --> 06:49.449
so I feel like I'll get it
on the day, you know.

06:49.552 --> 06:51.352
Maybe you should start
with something funny,

06:51.454 --> 06:53.651
so you're not, like,
immediately in tears.

06:53.753 --> 06:56.552
But it's kind of sweet.
It's endearing.

06:56.654 --> 06:57.951
Yeah, but you wanna look good.

06:58.053 --> 06:59.258
Crying makes you look
kind of ugly.

06:59.361 --> 07:01.756
-What?
-You, the general you.

07:01.858 --> 07:02.989
-Like, women.
-(SIGHS SOFTLY)

07:03.091 --> 07:05.464
Um, what about
the first time you met?

07:05.566 --> 07:07.332
Wasn't that
kind of a funny story?

07:07.434 --> 07:09.136
I love that book. I just...

07:09.238 --> 07:11.332
Oh, no, she can't tell that one.

07:11.434 --> 07:12.436
Why not?

07:12.538 --> 07:14.108
What stories are you gonna do?

07:14.210 --> 07:15.237
What do you mean? For my speech?

07:15.339 --> 07:16.442
Yeah.

07:16.544 --> 07:18.411
Well, you'll just
have to wait and see.

07:18.513 --> 07:20.146
No, no, no.
So we don't, you know,

07:20.248 --> 07:22.976
like, say the same things.

07:23.078 --> 07:24.651
Are you gonna use
the first time we met?

07:25.183 --> 07:26.320
Yes.

07:26.422 --> 07:27.648
Okay, well,
what about the first date?

07:27.750 --> 07:29.753
-Yeah, of course.
-Fuck!

07:29.855 --> 07:32.289
(CHUCKLES)
You don't have to do a speech.

07:32.391 --> 07:34.254
(SIGHS) First kiss?

07:34.356 --> 07:36.858
EMMA: Wait, so you can just,
like, go in whenever?

07:36.960 --> 07:38.025
CHARLIE: Yeah,
I do it all the time.

07:38.127 --> 07:39.461
EMMA: Oh, so you bring
all the girls here?

07:39.563 --> 07:40.960
CHARLIE: Um, yeah.

07:41.062 --> 07:42.796
-(EMMA SCOFFS, LAUGHS) Ouch.
-No,

07:42.898 --> 07:44.097
when I'm working late and stuff.

07:44.199 --> 07:45.632
Yeah, when you're working late
and stuff.

07:45.734 --> 07:47.404
-Yeah.
-(SIGHS)

07:47.506 --> 07:48.607
Okay, this is like...

07:48.709 --> 07:49.973
This is like a childhood dream,
you know,

07:50.075 --> 07:54.549
like sneaking into a mall
or a library at night. It's...

07:56.552 --> 07:58.713
Well, your dreams
are about to come true.

07:58.816 --> 08:00.654
-Wow.
-(BOTH CHUCKLE SOFTLY)

08:03.126 --> 08:04.691
-(RATTLING)
-Um...

08:05.754 --> 08:06.925
Is it not working?

08:07.027 --> 08:08.191
Hm.

08:08.293 --> 08:09.289
(BEEPING)

08:12.232 --> 08:14.201
(RATTLING)

08:14.303 --> 08:16.703
-(ALARM BLARING)
-Oh, sh...

08:17.468 --> 08:19.574
Um... Ooh!

08:23.672 --> 08:25.978
(DOORS THUDDING)

08:26.081 --> 08:28.011
(GRUNTING)

08:32.155 --> 08:34.354
(ALARM GROWS MUFFLED)

08:34.456 --> 08:37.889
(MUFFLED ALARM
CONTINUES BLARING)

08:40.427 --> 08:42.561
Wait, so he trapped you?

08:42.663 --> 08:45.158
It wasn't planned, Rachel.
(CHUCKLES)

08:45.260 --> 08:46.930
What about that time
you thought you had a...

08:47.032 --> 08:48.563
-(CONTINUES INDISTINCTLY)
-(MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING)

08:48.665 --> 08:50.235
(MACHINERY WHIRRING)

08:50.337 --> 08:52.673
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

09:02.846 --> 09:04.518
-ALICE: Who was that?
-Hm?

09:04.620 --> 09:07.648
Oh, uh, it's just Charlie.
I left my wallet.

09:07.750 --> 09:09.117
Hm. Who's Charlie?

09:09.219 --> 09:12.654
Uh, he's my boyfriend, I guess.
(CHUCKLES SOFTLY)

09:12.756 --> 09:14.290
(INTRIGUING MUSIC PLAYING)

09:14.393 --> 09:15.960
(CHUCKLES)

09:17.462 --> 09:18.795
Are you okay?

09:18.897 --> 09:21.097
Yeah. No, I'm fine.
(CHUCKLES SOFTLY)

09:24.306 --> 09:26.135
(EMMA BREATHING HEAVILY)

09:28.605 --> 09:30.477
(INHALES DEEPLY)

09:30.579 --> 09:31.707
ALICE: I don't know.
 Can you just...

09:31.810 --> 09:33.247
 She's saying it's her chest...

09:33.349 --> 09:34.741
It's her heart. Her heart is...

09:34.843 --> 09:36.382
So what was it?

09:36.484 --> 09:38.948
It was just, like, feelings.

09:39.050 --> 09:41.419
-Feelings? What do you mean?
-EMMA: Yeah.

09:41.521 --> 09:42.587
Like intense butterflies.

09:42.689 --> 09:43.653
-Right?
-RACHEL: No, I get that,

09:43.755 --> 09:46.059
but it wasn't your first time.

09:46.161 --> 09:47.428
I don't know.

09:47.530 --> 09:50.129
So you're saying
Charlie is your first...

09:50.231 --> 09:51.861
Love... Yeah.

09:51.963 --> 09:54.361
Your first love
or your first crush?

09:56.600 --> 09:57.804
Both, I think.

09:58.672 --> 10:00.508
-What, is that insane?
-At 30?

10:00.610 --> 10:03.208
Well, I mean,
I was 28 when we met, so...

10:03.310 --> 10:04.272
RACHEL: Still!

10:05.513 --> 10:07.509
I don't know. I used to be ugly.

10:07.611 --> 10:09.046
Oh, come on!

10:09.778 --> 10:11.185
Don't freak out,

10:11.287 --> 10:12.853
but there's a giant spider

10:12.955 --> 10:15.650
that's crawling up your back
and it's almost into your hair.

10:15.752 --> 10:17.087
Just don't panic.

10:20.590 --> 10:21.523
Nothing?

10:21.625 --> 10:22.893
-No.
-No.

10:22.995 --> 10:24.991
I feel like
you just have to do it louder.

10:25.093 --> 10:26.998
(MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING FAINTLY)

10:29.204 --> 10:31.165
Okay. Um...

10:31.267 --> 10:33.873
(WHISPERING)
I love you so much it hurts.

10:34.838 --> 10:36.337
I can't be without you.

10:37.679 --> 10:39.676
It's scary
'cause I can't imagine...

10:39.778 --> 10:45.645
(CHARLIE CONTINUES, MUFFLED)

10:45.747 --> 10:49.284
(WHISPERING) I want to marry you
but I'm too afraid to even ask.

10:52.823 --> 10:54.157
I think I caught that.

10:55.625 --> 10:56.797
You did?

10:57.628 --> 10:58.799
A hairy knife?

10:59.266 --> 11:00.262
A what?

11:00.364 --> 11:02.198
Did you say something
about, like, a hairy knife?

11:03.436 --> 11:04.970
-No.
-No?

11:05.969 --> 11:07.140
Emma, that's not even a thing.

11:07.242 --> 11:08.710
(BOTH LAUGH)

11:09.442 --> 11:10.404
(SNIFFLES)

11:11.080 --> 11:12.311
You okay?

11:12.413 --> 11:14.848
Yeah. No, it's good.

11:14.950 --> 11:16.910
Oh, come on, you gotta be
a bit more specific than that.

11:17.012 --> 11:18.114
Yeah, it's a little corny

11:18.216 --> 11:20.685
in a wedding speech kind of way,
but it's, um...

11:20.787 --> 11:23.190
All the pieces are there,
you know.

11:23.292 --> 11:23.952
I think you have it.

11:24.054 --> 11:25.490
-(SNIFFLES)
-(CHARLIE WHEEZES)

11:25.592 --> 11:26.757
All right, you can't cry

11:26.859 --> 11:28.360
-and say it sucks.
-(MIKE LAUGHS)

11:28.462 --> 11:29.829
(SPEAKER CRACKLING)

11:29.931 --> 11:32.096
 (I WANT TO LAY WITH YOU
BY SHIRA SMALLS PLAYING)

11:33.930 --> 11:35.803
And looking at each other.

11:44.908 --> 11:47.111
(CHARLIE AND EMMA GIGGLE)

11:48.777 --> 11:49.949
Nice.

11:55.390 --> 11:58.188
Slide... and two.

12:03.297 --> 12:04.260
Nice.

12:07.896 --> 12:10.365
And kiss. Great.

12:12.935 --> 12:14.735
Ready and drag.

12:14.837 --> 12:16.107
Step, step.

12:16.675 --> 12:18.475
Step, step. Drag.

12:18.577 --> 12:19.814
Step, step.

12:20.876 --> 12:22.113
And under.

12:24.187 --> 12:25.745
And arm up.

12:25.847 --> 12:27.019
Good.

12:31.094 --> 12:32.057
Playing.

12:35.496 --> 12:38.960
Ready and left arm.

12:39.062 --> 12:42.400
Down, up, up. Down, up, up.

12:42.502 --> 12:43.667
And switch.

12:43.769 --> 12:45.306
(CHARLIE GRUNTS SOFTLY)

12:45.408 --> 12:46.401
(CHARLIE GROANS SOFTLY)

12:48.605 --> 12:49.971
Oh.

12:50.073 --> 12:51.674
-EMMA: Oh?
-(BOTH CHUCKLE)

12:51.776 --> 12:53.406
INSTRUCTOR: Good.

12:53.508 --> 12:56.884
And this time, Emma,
go around a full circle.

12:58.617 --> 13:00.217
(LAUGHING)

13:02.017 --> 13:03.290
INSTRUCTOR: Great.

13:03.392 --> 13:05.860
Ready and step.

13:06.756 --> 13:07.994
And turn.

13:08.560 --> 13:09.556
And step.

13:10.331 --> 13:11.659
And turn.

13:11.761 --> 13:13.131
And step.

13:14.736 --> 13:19.104
Ready and drag,
step, step, in.

13:19.769 --> 13:21.073
Turn out.

13:22.376 --> 13:23.372
Good.

13:33.221 --> 13:34.048
Oh.

13:34.151 --> 13:36.052
-(BOTH LAUGH)
-Nearly there.

13:36.154 --> 13:37.685
INSTRUCTOR: Okay, not bad.
EMMA: Okay.

13:37.787 --> 13:39.486
Not bad.

13:39.588 --> 13:41.593
Still a little difficulty
in the middle section,

13:41.695 --> 13:43.024
but overall much better.

13:43.126 --> 13:44.398
EMMA: Yeah.
CHARLIE: Thanks.

13:44.500 --> 13:45.764
Let's just do it again?

13:45.866 --> 13:47.297
-Okay.
-EMMA: (WHISPERING) Okay.

13:47.863 --> 13:49.035
What?

13:50.770 --> 13:52.005
I just... I don't know,

13:52.107 --> 13:53.406
I feel like we should
just dance normally, right?

13:53.508 --> 13:54.540
What do you mean?

13:54.642 --> 13:56.438
Well, just the... (SIGHS)

13:56.540 --> 13:59.307
I don't know, it kinda
feels a little performative.

13:59.410 --> 14:01.913
It's a wedding.
It's performative by nature.

14:02.015 --> 14:03.717
Yeah. I think
if we just do it...

14:03.819 --> 14:05.113
(SMACKS LIPS)
...a couple more times,

14:05.215 --> 14:06.615
I'm gonna get it perfect,
I swear.

14:06.717 --> 14:08.717
INSTRUCTOR: I can't make up new
choreography right on the spot.

14:08.819 --> 14:10.051
CHARLIE: Yeah.

14:10.153 --> 14:12.587
Okay, well, just hear me out.

14:12.689 --> 14:14.354
-Hear me out. Please. Please.
-CHARLIE: No, Emma. Please.

14:14.456 --> 14:16.760
-Please, please, please.
-CHARLIE: Emma.

14:16.862 --> 14:18.031
