19:34.513 --> 19:36.112
This is about an ex-girlfriend
I was dating

19:36.214 --> 19:37.210
when I was in college.

19:37.312 --> 19:38.552
Who, Tessa?

19:38.654 --> 19:39.415
MIKE: Yeah.

19:39.517 --> 19:41.722
So, we'd been dating
for about a year,

19:41.824 --> 19:43.188
and it was her birthday,

19:43.290 --> 19:45.421
so we went down to Mexico
to celebrate,

19:45.523 --> 19:47.657
and she, look,
she had anger issues,

19:47.759 --> 19:49.960
and she didn't really
seem grateful for the trip,

19:50.062 --> 19:51.264
and we argued a lot.

19:51.366 --> 19:53.261
-It was really exhausting...
-Don't sugarcoat it.

19:53.363 --> 19:54.597
Okay, I'm just saying,

19:54.699 --> 19:57.671
you know, the vibes
were already off, all right?

19:57.773 --> 19:58.798
So, okay, anyway,

19:58.900 --> 20:01.073
um, one night we're walking home
from a bar.

20:01.175 --> 20:02.841
This was actually
on her birthday.

20:02.943 --> 20:05.412
Um, yeah, and, uh...

20:05.514 --> 20:08.313
we're cutting through this
back alley to get to our place,

20:08.415 --> 20:13.320
and this dog comes
out of nowhere, barking.

20:13.422 --> 20:17.557
And no owner in sight.
Just a wild, crazy street dog.

20:17.660 --> 20:19.224
And, um...

20:19.326 --> 20:22.295
instinctively,
she starts kicking at it,

20:22.397 --> 20:24.729
which only makes the dog
more aggressive, and...

20:24.831 --> 20:25.559
Right.

20:25.661 --> 20:27.932
...it actually
starts biting her.

20:28.034 --> 20:29.695
And what did you do?

20:29.797 --> 20:32.435
-(CHARLIE CHUCKLES SOFTLY)
-Um...

20:32.537 --> 20:33.800
I kinda sorta
just moved behind...

20:33.902 --> 20:35.908
-He used her as a human shield.
-No! I...

20:36.010 --> 20:36.802
That's what you said.

20:36.904 --> 20:38.704
