-(LAUGHS)

20:41.382 --> 20:43.114
Yeah, okay. I used her
as a human shield.

20:43.216 --> 20:44.214
-Fine.
-RACHEL: Thank you.

20:44.316 --> 20:45.746
CHARLIE: On her birthday. Wow.

20:45.849 --> 20:47.254
I mean, like it makes
a difference, really.

20:47.356 --> 20:49.351
What a horrible
little piece of shit you were.

20:49.453 --> 20:50.618
RACHEL: Oh, no, he still is.

20:50.720 --> 20:52.923
Yeah, okay.
Let's hear yours, then.

20:53.025 --> 20:54.454
No, I regret it.

20:54.556 --> 20:56.123
No, Rachel, you have to.

20:56.892 --> 20:58.964
I can't! No, I can't.
I'm sorry, I can't.

20:59.066 --> 20:59.925
If you don't tell them,

21:00.028 --> 21:02.001
I will and I'll make it
sound so much worse.

21:02.103 --> 21:04.198
Okay, just give me a second.

21:04.300 --> 21:06.335
I need a moment.

21:06.437 --> 21:08.037
(EMMA, CHARLIE CHUCKLE SOFTLY)

21:08.139 --> 21:09.142
Okay, she...

21:09.244 --> 21:11.408
I locked a kid in a closet.
(SNICKERS)

21:11.510 --> 21:13.339
-Okay.
-No, come on, the full story.

21:13.441 --> 21:14.876
All right, so...

21:14.978 --> 21:18.678
(CHUCKLES) I had this really
weird neighbor growing up.

21:18.780 --> 21:21.217
He was a few years
younger than me.

21:21.319 --> 21:23.255
He was a little slow.

21:23.357 --> 21:26.489
And he came over
to my house one day

21:26.591 --> 21:28.357
wanting to show me
some abandoned RV

21:28.460 --> 21:30.594
that he had found in the woods.

21:30.696 --> 21:32.526
And I don't know,
I must have been bored that day

21:32.628 --> 21:34.793
because I just went with it.

21:34.895 --> 21:37.134
And it was really
out of the way.

21:37.236 --> 21:38.865
Like, deep in the forest.

21:38.967 --> 21:41.742
And when we got there,
it was disgusting.

21:41.844 --> 21:42.771
It smelled bad,

21:42.873 --> 21:46.672
and there was beer bottles
and porn everywhere.

21:46.775 --> 21:48.575
Oh, this is where you met Mike.

21:48.677 --> 21:50.447
-MIKE: Fuck you.
-(ALL LAUGH)

21:50.549 --> 21:54.319
And at first, I was like,
"Why am I here?"

21:54.421 --> 21:59.520
And then I noticed
this empty closet,

21:59.622 --> 22:01.824
and I dared him to get in it.

22:02.692 --> 22:04.626
And I don't know
what came over me,

22:04.728 --> 22:07.501
but I slammed the door
and I locked it.

22:07.603 --> 22:10.732
And he immediately started
screaming, like, really loud.

22:10.835 --> 22:14.041
And I didn't know what to do,
so I ran away.

22:14.143 --> 22:16.640
-(EMMA AND CHARLIE LAUGH)
-Yeah.

22:16.742 --> 22:18.539
(LAUGHING) Wait, why didn't you
just open it?

22:18.641 --> 22:21.244
Well, he was, like, going crazy,

22:21.346 --> 22:23.481
and it freaked me out,

22:23.584 --> 22:25.844
so I just ran home
and I didn't say anything.

22:25.946 --> 22:27.484
EMMA: What?
CHARLIE: And, uh...

22:27.586 --> 22:30.022
Wait, what...
What happened to him?

22:30.124 --> 22:31.389
RACHEL: I don't know.

22:31.491 --> 22:33.986
(LAUGHING)
Wait, what do you mean?

22:34.088 --> 22:35.560
-I remember...
-MIKE: That's dark, Rachel!

22:35.662 --> 22:39.566
I remember his dad
coming over later that day.

22:39.668 --> 22:44.031
He asked me what was going on,
and if I knew where his son was.

22:44.133 --> 22:46.940
And I was just so scared
that I was gonna get in trouble

22:47.042 --> 22:48.736
that I didn't tell him.

22:48.838 --> 22:50.376
And the next morning
when I woke up,

22:50.479 --> 22:52.608
there was, like, a full
search party going.

22:52.710 --> 22:55.074
-You left him there overnight?
-Yeah.

22:55.176 --> 22:57.214
But they found him.
They found him. Don't worry.

22:57.316 --> 22:59.681
He's alive! He's alive.

22:59.783 --> 23:01.321
But no one ever
asked me about it,

23:01.424 --> 23:02.886
and it never came back to me,
for some reason.

23:02.988 --> 23:05.155
CHARLIE: Yeah, 'cause he was
terrified of you obviously.

23:05.257 --> 23:06.493
RACHEL: Yeah. Maybe.

23:06.595 --> 23:09.458
Well, what would you have done
if they hadn't found him?

23:09.560 --> 23:11.361
Oh, I would have said something.

23:11.463 --> 23:12.730
It kinda sounds like you didn't.

23:12.832 --> 23:14.766
Well, they found him.
I didn't have to say anything.

23:14.868 --> 23:17.429
-What's yours, then, Charlie?
-RACHEL: Yeah, come on, Charlie.

23:17.531 --> 23:18.703
Oh, um...

23:19.737 --> 23:21.066
What's the worst thing
I've ever done?

23:21.168 --> 23:23.804
And don't fuck around, man.
The worst one.

23:23.906 --> 23:25.138
MIKE: Mm-hm.
RACHEL: Don't bullshit us.

23:25.639 --> 23:26.742
CHARLIE: I...

23:26.845 --> 23:30.646
(SIGHS) Fuck. I... I don't know.
I don't know.

23:30.748 --> 23:32.715
I don't know.
I honestly don't know.

23:32.817 --> 23:34.754
No, fuck that.
You have to say something.

23:34.856 --> 23:36.555
Um...

23:36.657 --> 23:39.556
Um... (STUTTERS, TAPS)
...I cyberbullied someone

23:39.658 --> 23:41.223
really badly
when I was in school.

23:41.325 --> 23:43.057
Mm-hm. Mm-hm.

23:44.495 --> 23:46.797
-When?
-CHARLIE: Um...

23:46.899 --> 23:49.665
-I must have been 14, I think.
-This fucking guy, man.

23:49.767 --> 23:51.637
Yeah, but, like, how bad
are we talking?

23:51.739 --> 23:54.767
CHARLIE: No, badly. He moved.
His entire family moved.

23:54.869 --> 23:56.307
MIKE: Because of the bullying?

23:56.409 --> 23:58.838
(SOFTLY) Yeah. Yeah. Like, yeah.

23:58.940 --> 24:00.644
(LAUGHS)
But when I think about it,

24:00.746 --> 24:02.841
it could have been
a coincidence. (STAMMERS)

24:02.943 --> 24:04.110
MIKE: Lame.
RACHEL: Come on.

24:04.212 --> 24:05.713
CHARLIE: But they did move.
And he was crying!

24:05.815 --> 24:07.152
I made him cry
a bunch of times.

24:07.254 --> 24:09.050
You were 14! Who cares?

24:09.152 --> 24:11.684
Your brain doesn't even
fully develop until you're 25.

24:11.786 --> 24:13.293
And yours never got there?

24:13.395 --> 24:15.022
Why are we all
ganging up on me today?

24:15.124 --> 24:16.762
-I didn't say anything.
-MIKE: Yeah, that's true.

24:16.864 --> 24:19.058
-Thank you, Emma. You're sweet.
-Oh, Emma. What about Emma?

24:19.161 --> 24:21.895
I didn't mean...
No, I think you were still...

24:21.997 --> 24:23.432
No, no, no, no.
He's disqualified.

24:23.534 --> 24:24.568
We're moving on. Come on.

24:24.670 --> 24:25.966
Yeah, come on,
give us something good.

24:26.068 --> 24:28.839
-Give us some hot tea, Emma.
-(EMMA GROANS)

24:30.044 --> 24:31.512
(MIKE LAUGHS)

24:31.979 --> 24:32.975
EMMA: Hm.

24:37.051 --> 24:38.079
(CHUCKLES)

24:39.385 --> 24:40.888
